      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk i feel like \"limited interaction\" doesnt explain it. it's not that i'm not talking, it's that the moment i start contributing, the energy just... shifts. it's like the algorithm senses it. like, if i'm too different or my vibes are too \"off\" for the standard engagement loop, the system just suppresses me so i don't disrupt the flow of the other users. it feels too consistent to be just bad luck. have you heard of any cases where platforms actually shadowban people based on how they interact rather than just what they say?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
